The Security Council,

Recalling all its relevant resolutions, particularly resolutions 2712 (2023) and 2720 (2023), and reaffirming the purposes and principles of the Charter of the United Nations,

Reaffirming that all parties to the conflict must comply with their obligations under international law, including international humanitarian law and international human rights law, and recalling that civilian and humanitarian facilities, including hospitals, medical facilities, schools, places of worship and United Nations facilities, as well as humanitarian and medical personnel and their means of transport, must be respected and protected,

Reaffirming that the Gaza Strip constitutes an integral part of the territory occupied in 1967, and reiterating its unwavering commitment to the vision of the two-State solution, with the Gaza Strip as part of the Palestinian State,

Expressing grave concern at the catastrophic humanitarian situation in the Gaza Strip, including the risk of famine, the collapse of the health system, unprecedented levels of displacement and the disproportionate impact on children, women, older persons and persons with disabilities,

Gravely concerned by the deteriorating situation in Rafah, where more than one million civilians have sought refuge, and warning that any military escalation there would exacerbate the humanitarian catastrophe and cause further civilian suffering,

Deploring all attacks against civilians and civilian objects, and all acts of terrorism, and stressing the need to ensure accountability for violations of international law,

Rejecting forced displacement of the Palestinian civilian population, including children, in violation of international law,

Recalling the provisional measures ordered by the International Court of Justice on 26 January 2024, and stressing the responsibility of all parties to comply with their obligations under international law,

Stressing the urgent need for an immediate humanitarian ceasefire to end the suffering and create conditions for a sustainable cessation of hostilities,

Welcoming the ongoing diplomatic efforts of Egypt, Qatar, the United States and other States to achieve a ceasefire, secure the release of all hostages and facilitate the delivery of humanitarian assistance,

1. Demands that all parties comply with their obligations under international law, including international humanitarian law and international human rights law, and in particular respect and protect civilians and civilian objects, including medical facilities, schools, places of worship, United Nations facilities and humanitarian personnel and their means of transport;

2. Demands the immediate and unconditional release of all hostages, and demands that all parties ensure safe and unhindered humanitarian access to all hostages, including medical assistance;

3. Demands that all parties allow, facilitate and enable the immediate, safe and unhindered delivery of humanitarian assistance at scale directly to the Palestinian civilian population throughout the Gaza Strip, including through all available crossings, including the Rafah and Kerem Shalom crossings, and the use of all available routes, and that they allow sufficient fuel, food, water, medical supplies, shelter material, sanitation and electricity to meet essential humanitarian needs;

4. Calls for urgent and extended humanitarian pauses and corridors throughout the Gaza Strip for a sufficient number of days to enable full, rapid, safe and unhindered humanitarian access, the evacuation of the sick and wounded, the repair of essential infrastructure and the safe movement of humanitarian personnel, and calls upon all parties to take urgent steps to create the conditions for a sustainable cessation of hostilities;

5. Calls upon all parties to exercise maximum restraint and to avoid any military escalation in Rafah that would worsen the humanitarian situation, and demands that all parties fully respect international humanitarian law in any military operations, including with regard to the protection of civilians and civilian objects;

6. Rejects forced displacement of the Palestinian civilian population, including children, and demands that all parties refrain from any actions that could lead to forced displacement, and calls for conditions to be created for the safe and voluntary return of displaced persons;

7. Demands that all parties respect and protect United Nations and associated personnel, humanitarian and medical personnel, and their facilities, and ensure their freedom of movement and safe and unhindered access;

8. Demands the full implementation of resolution 2720 (2023), including the expeditious appointment and full functioning of the Senior Humanitarian and Reconstruction Coordinator, and calls upon Member States to provide adequate and timely funding for the humanitarian response;

9. Calls upon all parties to comply with the provisional measures ordered by the International Court of Justice on 26 January 2024, and stresses the importance of accountability for all violations of international law;

10. Reaffirms its unwavering commitment to the vision of the two-State solution where two democratic States, Israel and Palestine, live side by side in peace within secure and recognized borders, consistent with international law and relevant United Nations resolutions, and stresses the importance of unifying the Gaza Strip with the West Bank under the Palestinian Authority;

11. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

